---
import { u } from '../lib/url';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  section="Page"
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  kicker="Legal"
  description="The terms for using this site: what it is, what you can do with its content, and the limits on liability."
  wide={false}
>
  <div class="prose-nw">
    <p class="text-faint"><em>Last updated: 18 September 2026</em></p>

    <p>
      This is a personal portfolio site. Using it means you agree to the terms below. There is no
      account to create and nothing here is a paid service.
    </p>

    <h2>Use of the site</h2>
    <p>
      You're welcome to browse, read, and link to anything here. Don't scrape the site to republish
      it wholesale, attempt to disrupt it, or use the <a href={u('/contact/')}>contact form</a> to spam
      or phish.
    </p>

    <h2>Content and ownership</h2>
    <p>
      Writing, project write-ups, and site design are mine unless otherwise credited. Code samples
      and open-source projects follow the license in their own repository. Publications linked from
      this site belong to their respective journals and are shared only via DOI links.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided as-is. Research summaries, project descriptions, and figures reflect my
      best understanding at the time of writing but are not a substitute for the underlying
      published work, which is linked wherever it exists.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party links</h2>
    <p>
      Links to external sites — journals, GitHub, Cal.com, Formspree, and similar — are provided for
      convenience. I don't control and am not responsible for their content or availability.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated as the site changes. The date at the top of this page reflects the
      last revision.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms can go to <a href="mailto:noah@noahweidig.com"
        >noah@noahweidig.com</a
      >. See also the <a href={u('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
